# CLCPA-85 fixtures are byte-exact inputs, not source.
#
# a1-2023-lf-bom.csv exists to prove the parser handles LF-only files and a
# UTF-8 BOM. Git normalisation would rewrite it to CRLF on checkout, so that
# assertion would pass on a fresh clone for the wrong reason: the file it
# tested would no longer exist. -text stops git touching the bytes.
*.csv -text
